Step 0 already exposes the central issue: the paper itself states that solvability of \(w(x,y)=u\) is decidable in polynomial time, so a Track A claim would be false. I’m now checking whether the paper supports an honest Track B family—i.e., whether the standard method is mechanically large at a writable shipping size while a short Nielsen-automorphism insight gives a compact witness.
