diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b2de206a57e7dd6db2c293feaec2641458219161
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,142 @@
+# Free-group word equations from arXiv:0705.4246
+
+| profile | value |
+|---|---|
+| Track | **B — no-tool compression** |
+| Native domain | algebra |
+| Object regime | finite discrete |
+| Computational core | other (free-group word equation) |
+| Certificate | exact symbolic pair of group words |
+| Intuition | change of variables via a Nielsen matrix |
+| Domain essentiality | native; no reduction |
+
+## What the family asks
+
+An instance gives a word `w(x,y)` and a target word `u` in the free group
+`F(a,b)`.  The solver must provide concrete words `x,y` of stated lengths and
+letter multiplicities such that substitution into `w`, followed by free
+reduction, equals `u`.  The checker performs only exact substitution, stack
+reduction, count checks, and string comparison.  This is the paper's native
+object and definition, not a graph or finite-field surrogate.  Source:
+[Nicholas Touikan, *The equation w(x,y)=u over free groups*](https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.4246).
+
+Generation starts with the solution calculated in Section 3 for
+`w0=[x,y]^2 x`, applies the fixed rational equivalence `x -> xy`, and then
+applies sampled elementary Nielsen transformations.  Definition 2.15 and
+Lemma 2.16 guarantee that the carried pair remains a solution.  Thus the
+generator knows the witness before it forms the emitted equation.
+
+## Why Track B
+
+Track A would be false.  The introduction cites Ciobanu's polynomial-time
+algorithm for the rank-two endomorphism problem, and Lemma 2.17 makes Nielsen
+reduction effective.  The executable reference implementation literally tries
+the two inverse Nielsen shears while shortening the full word; on the hard
+shipping preset it solved 8/8 instances using 154,067 word-symbol scans in
+0.240 seconds total (19,258 scans per instance), with distribution-specific
+cost `O(n|w|)`.
+
+The compact route uses the abelianized exponent-sum pair.  It is the sum of the
+columns of a nonnegative unimodular matrix.  A Bezout identity recovers those
+columns, Euclidean subtraction factors the matrix into Nielsen shears, and the
+Section 3 pair is transported backwards.  The measured maximum was 142 exact
+operations.  Section 2.1's easy cases are avoided: the Section 3 word is not
+primitive, and its exponent-sum gcd is one, so it is not a proper power.  The
+target is nontrivial and the planted pair is noncommuting, hence rank two.
+
+## Worked demo
+
+With `seed=0`, the complete small instance is:
+
+```text
+w(x,y) = xyxxyXYxyXYXYXXYX
+u      = baBAbaBB
+sigma(w) = (-2,-1)
+x: length 5, counts [a,A,b,B] = [1,2,1,1]
+y: length 6, counts [a,A,b,B] = [2,1,2,1]
+```
+
+The answer is `{"x":"aBAbA","y":"aBabbA"}`.
+`verify(inst, inst["answer"])` returns `(True, "ok")`; deleting the last
+letter of `x` returns `(False, "x must have length 5")`.  This rung is small
+enough to solve and check by hand by trying the two one-step inverse Nielsen
+changes.
+
+## Presets
+
+| preset | Nielsen depth `n` | minimum direction switches | target exponent choices | answer cap | status |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| demo | 1 | 0 | 1 | 32 | hand example |
+| easy | 7 | 3 | 3 | 150 | oracle pending |
+| medium | 9 | 5 | 4 | 220 | oracle pending |
+| hard | 10 | 6 | 4 | 250 | current candidate shipping preset |
+
+## Local gates
+
+| gate | result | measurement |
+|---|---|---|
+| G1 | pass | 16/16 planted witnesses verified |
+| G2 | pass | 5/5 corruptions rejected with 5 distinct reasons |
+| G3 | pass | tagged JSON recovered through prose and a Markdown fence |
+| G4 | pass | 0/200,000 valid structure-aware multiset guesses |
+| G5 | pass | demo: 1/10,800 exact; hard density sample: 0/200,000; 256-restart attack failed in 0.062 s |
+| G6 | pass | four attacks at 0/8 each; reference and compact solvers at 8/8 |
+| G7 | pass | `n=20` built and verified; equation length grew from 657 to 15,247 |
+| G8 | pass | 60/60 relabellings invariant and witness-preserving; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct |
+| G9(c) | pass | 234 chars, 219 letters, 59 estimated tokens on the measured seed; exact preset maximum 66 tokens; 142 operations |
+
+The G4 sampler already enforces every stated length and exact `[a,A,b,B]`
+multiplicity.  The two finite dihedral quotients used to accelerate sampling
+only reject candidates: a quotient mismatch rigorously proves inequality, and
+every quotient match is sent to the exact verifier.
+
+## Oracle loop and G9 arms
+
+The required harness was invoked, but the configured OpenRouter account
+returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded` on every redraw before any valid oracle
+attempt.  The script therefore refused to make a hardness verdict, as it
+should.  Its error rows remain in `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl`; they are **not**
+evidence that a model failed the problem, and this result is not release-ready
+until the harness is rerun with quota.
+
+| arm | solved/valid attempts | conclusion |
+|---|---:|---|
+| bare | 0/0 | blocked by provider quota |
+| structural hint | 0/0 | not run |
+| placebo hint | 0/0 | not run |
+
+Consequently `hinted - placebo` is not yet measurable.  The structural hint
+names only the matrix invariant; it does not give Bezout reconstruction or the
+Euclidean procedure.
+
+## Use
+
+```python
+from gen_0705_4246 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, render, verify
+
+inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
+print(render(inst))
+assert verify(inst, inst["answer"]) == (True, "ok")
+```
+
+After a successful oracle rerun, emit from the repository root with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 0705.4246 20
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+The benchmark is easy with a free-group package or the implemented reference
+solver; that is the reason for Track B.  The sampled density is relative to
+uniform permutations of the disclosed multisets and is not a proof of
+uniqueness at hard size.  The demo is uniquely solved in its 10,800-element
+language.  The attack panel does not implement Ciobanu's complete algorithm or
+a general Whitehead automorphism search: it tests full-word L/R descent for the
+generated positive-Nielsen regime, plus frequency, target-prefix, random, and
+one-shear attacks.  `canonical_key` is complete for signed permutations and
+inversions of the two coefficient generators and two variables, but not for
+arbitrary Nielsen equivalence.  Most importantly, external multi-vendor
+hardness and both G9 comparison arms remain unmeasured because of provider
+quota; no shipping claim should be inferred until those files are replaced by
+successful script-owned runs.
