The native Track B Nielsen-transformation family passes all nine local gates, including:

- 0/200,000 structure-aware random guesses
- Four attacks at 0/8
- Reference algorithm solving 8/8 with 154,067 symbol scans
- Compact route requiring at most 142 operations
- 219-letter shipping witness, within all G9(c) caps

It is not release-ready because OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded` on every hardening redraw. These errors were correctly retained rather than counted as model failures; `submit.sh` therefore blocks at Step 4. No `REJECTED.md` was created because the family itself has not failed.

The oracle and G9 runs must be repeated after restoring OpenRouter quota.
