codex
Implementation is complete, but release verification is blocked by external quota.

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/gen_0705_4246.py) — native free-group equations, `TRACK = "B"`, exact verification.
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/selftest_report.json) — all nine local gates pass.
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/README.md) — paper triage, construction, measurements, example, and caveats.
- G4: 0/200,000 valid structure-aware guesses.
- G6: four attacks failed 0/8; reference algorithm solved 8/8 using 154,067 scans; compact route used at most 142 operations.
- Emit smoke test succeeded.

Track A was rejected because the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.4246) explicitly cites a polynomial-time solution algorithm. The construction instead uses its Section 3 solution and Nielsen transformations for an honest Track B compression problem.

The required oracle run failed with HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” on every redraw. Consequently, [the transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl) contains only error rows, and `submit.sh` correctly exits 8. No hardness verdict was fabricated, and no `REJECTED.md` was created.

Once OpenRouter quota is restored, rerun:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_0705_4246.py
```

The bare and both G9 arms must then be completed before release.
