codex
Implemented and verified the native free-group equation generator as Track B. It uses the paper’s Section 3 solution and transports it through Nielsen transformations justified by Lemma 2.16; Track A is excluded because the paper cites a polynomial-time decision algorithm. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/html/0705.4246v5)

Deliverables:

- [gen_0705_4246.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/gen_0705_4246.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/README.md)
- [bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [structural-hint transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/0705.4246/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four adversary attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Bare oracle: 0/3 solved at the shipping `easy` preset.
- Structural hint: 0/3; placebo: 0/3.
- Maximum shipping answer: 116 characters, 101 letters, approximately 29 tokens.
- Intended compact route: at most 121 exact operations.
- Twenty emitted instances all verify and have distinct canonical keys.

The submission validator passed through interface, native-domain, emission, and diversity checks. Its final commit/push phase was unavailable because the workspace is not a Git checkout.
